<title>HONG KONG: Top Glory nine-month net HK$165 mln.</title>
<headline>Top Glory nine-month net HK$165 mln.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-05-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nine months ended December 31</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	 9.0	 vs  3.4</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)  1.5	 vs  3.5</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	8.52 loss vs  5.00 loss</p>
<p>    Net			  165.00    vs  61.42</p>
<p>    Turnover		   955.29    vs  853.64</p>
<p>    Company name	     Top Glory International Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		June 17-23</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	 July 4</p>
<p>NOTE - Top Glory, controlled by China-backed China National Cereals Oil and Foodstuffs Import and Export Corp (Ceroil), engages in property investment and food related business.</p>
<p>The company changed its financial year-end to December 31 from March 31. Comparative figures are for April 1, 1995, to March 31, 1996.</p>
<p>Net is after an exceptional loss on provision for diminution in value of interest in short-term investments.</p>
<p>Total dividend for nine months is 1.5 H.K. cents vs 13.5 cents (for year).</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong newsroom (852) 2843 6441</p>
</text>
